@startuml validation-enforcement
' Where a check is enforced: the apiserver at apply time, or a reconciler
' after the object is stored. The outcomes of a reconcile-time rule are
' validation-outcomes.puml; the rule-to-outcome mapping is the table on
' docs/src/resources/validation-and-defaulting.md (the source of truth).
!include _style.puml

skinparam ConditionEndStyle hline
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10

|$agentBg|Developer|
|$ctrlBg|apiserver|
|$storeBg|etcd|
|$ctrlBg|Reconciler|

|Developer|
start
:kubectl apply;

|apiserver|
if (schema and CEL rules) then (violates)
  |Developer|
  :**rejected**\nthe object never exists; <<#FFCDD2>>
  kill
else (passes)
endif

|etcd|
:object stored;

|Reconciler|
:reconcile-time rules;
:status on the object;
stop
@enduml
